From b63e9cb8d3a1c1f4c1d8923e162c33344c5902a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:17:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: external VU1 backend hook and PS2X_VU1 selector

PS2ExternalVu1 (runtime/ps2_vu1_external.h, same shape as the external GS):
mscal(memory, startPC, top, itop, fbrst) and mscnt(memory, top, itop, fbrst)
return the D/T stop; setState/readState translate the architectural state.
When set, the VIF1 MSCAL/MSCALF and MSCNT callbacks call it instead of the
VU1 interpreter (with the PC sampler's vu1 flag set around the call), write
VPU_STAT D/T from its result, and feed PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE through readState.
syncCoreSubsystems hands it the interpreter's reset state.
PS2Runtime::vu1State() reads the active backend's registers. The backend
reads VU1 code/data and the code generation from PS2Memory and submits its
XGKICK packets to PS2Memory::submitGifPacket(Path1), as finishXgkick does.

PS2X_VU1=interp|mvu is read once in initialize (unset = interp; mvu needs a
build with PS2X_EXTERNAL_VU1_DIR; unknown = "[vu1] unknown PS2X_VU1=...",
exit 2). CMake PS2X_EXTERNAL_VU1_DIR add_subdirectory's a library defining
ps2x_external_vu1 (after the external GS); PS2X_EXTERNAL_VU1=1 is a source
property of ps2_runtime.cpp only, so generated game code keeps its flags.
Null backend = unchanged behaviour.

Test: a recording backend set before the subsystems bind gets the reset
state, the MSCAL with start pc 0x40 and FBRST, its PATH1 packet reaches the
GIF arbiter byte for byte, the interpreter does not run, VPU_STAT takes its
T stop, MSCNT reaches it, and vu1State() returns its registers.
